.enriched-timestamps.json

# Logs & temp
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# 📓 PERSONAL CONTENT (the system is shareable, the journal is not)
# History audit found 8 daily notes had been committed and later deleted —
# deletion does not remove them from history, so these rules make the boundary
# structural instead of relying on never typing `git add -A`.
# MOCs and already-tracked showcase files stay tracked; everything else is isolated.
#
# The repository ROOT had a hole in this boundary: memory.md and handoff.md sat
# beside AGENTS.md and Home.md, matched no rule here, and were therefore tracked
# and published — carrying the owner's real name, location and timezone, role and
# stack, and the real filesystem paths of private projects. Ignore rules cannot
# fix that retroactively (they never apply to tracked files), so they are named
# explicitly and untracked in the same commit that adds them.
/memory.md
/handoff.md

00-Inbox/*
!00-Inbox/_*.md

01-Daily/*
!01-Daily/_*.md

02-Projects/*
!02-Projects/_*.md

03-Dev/*
!03-Dev/_*.md

04-Learning/*
!04-Learning/_*.md

05-Personal/*
!05-Personal/_*.md

06-Resources/Articles/*
06-Resources/Articles/**/*
!06-Resources/Articles/_*.md
!06-Resources/Articles/**/_*.md

06-Resources/Guides/*
06-Resources/Guides/**/*
!06-Resources/Guides/_*.md
!06-Resources/Guides/**/_*.md
# Distributable public guides needed by fresh clones:
!06-Resources/Guides/Setup & Configuration.md
!06-Resources/Guides/Documentation Index.md
!06-Resources/Guides/Hey Loey Guide.md
!06-Resources/Guides/Maintenance & Troubleshooting.md
!06-Resources/Guides/Onboarding.md
# Already-published guides. These entered the index before the folder rule above existed,
# and an ignore rule never untracks a file, so they are public either way — but silence
# about it is what let the owner-only records below the same rule publish unnoticed. Every
# negation here is a deliberate public declaration, and the publication-boundary coverage
# test (rule A) fails when a tracked path is matched by an ignore rule without one.
!06-Resources/Guides/CONTRIBUTING.md
!06-Resources/Guides/Mobile Workflow Guide.md
!06-Resources/Guides/Plugin Ownership.md
!06-Resources/Guides/QuickAdd Inbox Optimization Guide.md
!06-Resources/Guides/Second Brain Guide.md
!06-Resources/Guides/Tagging & Properties.md
!06-Resources/Guides/TypeScript Migration Feasibility Assessment.md
!06-Resources/Guides/Vault Security Policy.md
!06-Resources/Guides/Weekly AI Summary Guide.md
# Owner-only engineering records. NOT negated on purpose: they are private, declared in
# `.githooks/lib/private-records.txt`, and must never be tracked again.

07-Reviews/*
07-Reviews/**/*
!07-Reviews/_*.md
!07-Reviews/**/_*.md
!07-Reviews/Habit Analytics Dashboard.md

08-Concepts/*
08-Concepts/**/*
!08-Concepts/_*.md
!08-Concepts/**/_*.md

99-Attachments/*
99-Attachments/**/*
!99-Attachments/_*.md
!99-Attachments/**/_*.md
# The monthly folder must be re-included BEFORE the file rules below it. Git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is still excluded, which is why the two
# showcase negations that used to sit here had no effect at all and the four images were
# "tracked but ignored". Verified with `git check-ignore -v --no-index` on each file.
!99-Attachments/2026-08/
!99-Attachments/2026-08/obsidian-*.png
!99-Attachments/2026-08/file-20260803003355764.png
